# Windsurf Agent Rules — Jakarta Migration MCP

## Available MCP Servers
MCP servers are configured in `.mcp.json` at project root. Available servers:
- `gradle` — Run Gradle build/test/lint commands
- `github` — GitHub API access (issues, PRs, repos)
- `filesystem` — Read/write project files
- `sequentialthinking` — Structured reasoning
- `memory` — Cross-session context persistence
- `postgres` — PostgreSQL database access
- `codebase-indexer` — Codebase search and indexing

## Debugging Runtime Errors
1. Check service status: `docker compose ps` or `curl http://localhost:8080/actuator/health`
2. Enable debug mode: `LOG_LEVEL=debug`
3. Check Docker logs: `docker compose logs -f`
4. Review known issues: `docs/troubleshooting/COMMON_ISSUES.md`
5. Run fast tests after fix: `./gradlew fastTest`

## Logging
- All production logging must use SLF4J (`log.info`, `log.debug`, `log.warn`, `log.error`)
- Never use `System.out.println` in production code
- Respect `LOG_LEVEL` env var: debug, info, warn, error

## CI/CD Signal vs Confidence
- Signal (inner loop): compile → fast tests — run before every commit
- Confidence (CI only): integration → security → full matrix — run async in CI
- Validate pipeline config: `gh workflow run --dry-run`

## Fast Test Loop
- `./gradlew :community-core-engine:fastTest` — Quick core engine feedback (<15s)
- `./gradlew fastTest` — All module fast tests
- See `COMMANDS.md` for full command catalogue
